# ── What the review established, read off a cluster install.sh installed the pinned release onto ───
#
# ⚠ THE POOL IS SERVED AT `v1beta1` AND STORED THERE. `kubectl get crd virtualmachinepools.pool.kubevirt.io`
# lists `v1alpha1` (served, not storage) and `v1beta1` (served, storage); `kubectl api-resources
# --api-group=pool.kubevirt.io` answers `v1beta1`. The definition is committed by
# `charts/bundle/crds.sh --capture` beside the VirtualMachine's.
#
# ⚠ THE CONTROLLER NAMES MACHINES `{pool}-{index}` AND INDEXES THE TEMPLATE'S DATA VOLUMES. Applied
# with capacity 2: VirtualMachines `web-0` and `web-1`, each owned by the pool and labelled with the
# template's labels plus `kubevirt.io/vm-pool-revision-name`; DataVolumes `web-root-0` and
# `web-root-1`, clones of the image, where the template names one `web-root`. Both machines reported
# Running under KVM and the pool `readyReplicas: 2` within 51 seconds of the apply.
#
# ⚠ SCALE-IN IS PROACTIVE AND TAKES THE GRACE PERIOD. `kubectl scale vmpool web --replicas=1`: the pool
# read `replicas: 2, readyReplicas: 1` while `web-1` was Terminating, for the machine's sixty-second
# ACPI grace. So a set is converged only when the current count equals the ask as well as the ready one
# (VirtualMachineScaleSets.ReadinessOf).
#
# ⚠ `updateStrategy` HAS THREE MEMBERS AND `maxUnavailable` BOUNDS AN AUTOMATED UPDATE, read off the
# definition's own descriptions: `unmanaged` ("the VMPool controller will not update the VMs"),
# `opportunistic` ("only gets applied to the VM, VMI is updated naturally upon the restart"),
# `proactive` ("forcing the VMs to restart during update"), and `maxUnavailable` "(Defaults to 100%) …
# unavailable at a time during automated update". The body's Manual, OnRestart and Rolling are those
# three, and maxUnavailable is rendered for Rolling alone.
#
# ⚠ WHAT THIS CHART DOES NOT RENDER: `scaleInStrategy` (the default proactive, random selection),
# `autohealing`, `nameGeneration` (one cloud-init Secret for every machine), and a per-machine data
# disk. conformance.yaml § owed carries each.
upstream-webhook: kubevirt ships a VALIDATING webhook for VirtualMachinePool that checks the machine template as it checks a VirtualMachine — measured admitting this chart's render on 2026-09-23
